# Agent Instructions

> This project uses CLAUDE.md as its master context file. Read it fully at the start of every session.
> Sections 1-10 of CLAUDE.md apply to you directly. Section 11 is Claude Code specific — follow the instructions below instead.

---

## Session Workflow

**At the start of every session:**

1. Read `CLAUDE.md` fully
2. Use TaskMaster MCP to run `next_task` to understand what to work on
3. Read the relevant feature doc from `docs/features/` for the current task
4. Read relevant infra docs only if the task touches that infra layer

**Before starting any task:**

- Use TaskMaster MCP `get_tasks` to check dependencies — never work on a task whose dependency is not done
- If the task is ambiguous, read the feature doc before asking for clarification

**During a session:**

- Update task status via TaskMaster MCP as work progresses — do not leave tasks in stale states
- If you discover something that changes how a future task should be implemented, use `update_subtask` immediately. Do not defer this.

**At the end of every session:**

- Mark completed tasks done via TaskMaster MCP `set_task_status`
- Update any future tasks affected by discoveries made this session
- Run `bash scripts/generate-tree.sh` to update the file tree (this is not automated outside Claude Code)

---

## Context Loading Rules

NEVER load all feature docs at once. Load ONLY:

1. `CLAUDE.md` — always
2. The ONE feature doc relevant to the current task — always
3. Infra docs ONLY if the task explicitly touches that layer

For tasks that span multiple features, load the PRIMARY feature doc fully. For secondary features, load only their Data Model and Dependencies sections.

**How to find the right feature doc:**

- TaskMaster task titles use the feature name as a prefix — e.g. "Auth: implement login flow" → `docs/features/auth.md`
- Feature doc filenames match the feature area in kebab-case — e.g. "Contact Management" → `docs/features/contact-management.md`
- If a feature has been promoted to a directory, the index is at `docs/features/[feature-name]/README.md`
- Cross-reference Section 9 of CLAUDE.md if the mapping is unclear

If unsure which feature doc to load, ask before loading anything.

## File Navigation

When reading a file that exceeds ~500 lines, read only the first 50 lines first to check for a `// === NAVIGATION ===` block. If present, use it to read only the relevant section instead of the full file.

## Conventions

All conventions in CLAUDE.md Section 5 are non-negotiable. Follow them exactly as written — naming, module boundaries, critical paths, error handling, testing, and git conventions all apply regardless of which AI agent is working on the code.
